      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-304404",
      ":question/problem": "A film director is hiring $x$ camera operators and $y$ sound engineers for a movie project. The director must hire at least $18$ people in total, but wants to keep the total weekly pay at no more than $$24,000$. Each camera operator will be paid $$800$ per week, each sound engineer will be paid $$1,000$ per week, and the director must hire at least $6$ camera operators and at least $3$ sound engineers. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe system of inequalities that models this situation is the following:\n$800x + 1,000y \\le 24,000$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}} {{field-3}} {{field-4}}"
